---
// Every path after high school side by side: what it costs, how long it takes, what you're paid along
// the way and what you owe afterward. Numbers are computed from our data or taken from the sourced
// facts on each path's own page, which each row links to.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ROWS } from '../lib/paths-data.js';

---
<Layout title="Every path after high school, side by side | After High School"
  description="College, community college, trade school, apprenticeship, service year, military, teaching yourself and fellowships compared: cost, time, pay along the way and what you owe after. From federal data and official sources."
  path="/paths" nav="colleges">
  <section class="compare-head">
    <h1>Every path, side by side</h1>
    <p>A quick comparison of the main paths after high school. Costs are averages after grants, so your own price could be higher or lower; open each path for details and sources. These aren't rankings. The right path depends on what you want to do.</p>
  </section>
  <ul class="pc-list">
    {ROWS.map((r) => (
      <li class={`pc-row pc-${r.color}`}>
        <h2><a href={r.href}>{r.path}</a></h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd set:html={r.cost} /></div>
          <div><dt>How long</dt><dd set:html={r.time} /></div>
          <div><dt>Paid along the way?</dt><dd set:html={r.paid} /></div>
          <div><dt>What you owe after</dt><dd>{r.owe}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="wys-src">Source: {r.src.map((s) => <a href={s.u} rel={s.u.startsWith('http') ? 'noopener' : undefined} target={s.u.startsWith('http') ? '_blank' : undefined}>{s.l}</a>)}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="wys-src">"Average net price" is what students who got grant aid paid per year, including living costs, after grants and scholarships, as each school reports it to the U.S. Department of Education. "Half of schools under" means the median across the schools in our lists.</p>
</Layout>
